{# Webfonts for the whole site — include this FIRST inside every <head>.

   The fonts are self-hosted from /assets/fonts/ and the @font-face rules are inlined
   below. They used to be a <link> to fonts.googleapis.com, which was the site's only
   render-blocking resource: Lighthouse measured it at ~850ms of the critical path on
   every page. The browser had to open a third-party connection and fetch a stylesheet
   before it could even discover which font files it needed, so the fonts landed after
   first paint and the text repainted in them — LCP on article pages sat ~330ms behind
   FCP purely because of that swap.

   Keep the rules INLINE rather than in a stylesheet of their own. An extra
   <link rel="stylesheet"> would put a fresh render-blocking request back on the path,
   and the whole block is ~8KB that compresses to well under 1KB because the
   unicode-range strings repeat. Inlining also means the preload scanner sees the
   font URLs in the first chunk of HTML.

   The preloads cover only the faces that paint above the fold; see the PRELOAD note
   in src/libs/webfonts.js before adding more. Everything here is generated from the
   manifest in that file, so edit it there, not in this template.

   Every layout with its own <head> includes this: main.njk, index.njk, tulisan.njk,
   serial.njk, cv.njk, search.njk. If you add another layout, add it here too, or that
   page loses its webfonts. #}
{{ webfontPreloads | safe }}
<style>{{ webfontCss | safe }}</style>
